or><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>WATANABE YOSHITANE</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KANEKO, SHOICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOYAMA, YOSHINARI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUZUKI, KEITARO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKAHASHI, TAKESHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TANEGASHIMA, OSAMU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>WATANABE, YOSHITANE</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A transparent hard coating material curable with heat or ultraviolet which is suitable for forming on a substrate, such as a film or sheet, an antireflection film functioning to reduce external light reflection and heighten the transmittance of light and having a low refractive index. The transparent hard coating material comprises an ultraviolet- or heat-curable resin having one or more (meth)acryloyl groups per molecule and colloidal particles of a silica/magnesium fluoride hydrate composite. It gives a transparent cured film having a refractive index of 1.48 or lower.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un matériau de revêtement dur, transparent, durcissant sous l'effet de la chaleur ou d'un rayonnement ultraviolet, et conçu pour former sur un substrat, tel qu'un film ou une feuille, une couche mince antireflet destinée à réduire la réflexion de la lumière extérieure et à rehausser le coefficient de transmission de la lumière, et possédant un faible indice de réfraction. Ce matériau de revêtement dur, transparent, comprend une résine durcissant sous l'effet de la chaleur ou d'un rayonnement ultraviolet, laquelle comporte un ou plusieurs groupes (méth)acryloyle par molécule, ainsi que des particules colloïdales d'un composite d'hydraté de silice/magnésium fluoré. Ce matériau permet d'obtenir un film durci, transparent, possédant un indice de réfraction de l'ordre de 1,48 ou moins.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>